                <pb facs="0539" n="453" sameAs="frus:frus1927v01/pg453"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 2]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Declaration of Trustees of the Austrian Loan of
                        1923</hi></head>
                <p>The Trustees have heard the interesting exposé made by the Austrian delegation
                    and taken note of the statements made by Doctor Schuller concerning the
                    projected loan; as regards this loan the Trustees consider that they are not
                    concerned to express an opinion unless they consider that the projected loan is
                    likely to be prejudicial to the Austrian Government guaranteed loan 1923/43.
                    Therefore, when the terms and conditions of the loan are further advanced the
                    Trustees will be notified in time to enable them to consider whether these are
                    prejudicial to the interests of the bondholders of the Austrian Government
                    guaranteed loan 1923/43.</p>
            </div>
